{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/832092-if-demons-won-the-war","id":832092,"title":"If Demons \"Won\" the War","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-17T14:50:41-08:00","id":832092,"title":"If Demons \"Won\" the War","content":"The greatest trick the GM would ever play...<br /> <br /> What if Angel activity suddenly stopped. Nobody knows the reason why. New infrastructure never comes, Angels don't respond to Compromise, they don't even appear (except maybe those that were already exiles). How would demons respond? After days, months, years, of silence. This is the plot to a game I'm planning, where demons begin vying for control of Aether reserves, territory, and more. The question is, however, whether the GM is truly gone, or about to unleash something beyond mortal reckoning.<br /> <br /> Any ideas on what issues to tackle?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T15:19:56-08:00","id":832110,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't it become one hell of a struggle for dwindling resources, as all the Infrastructure slowly crumbles without repair? Aether is practically the lifeblood of the Unchained, and unless someone finds a way to build new Infrastructure without the Machine it'll quickly run out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T15:21:45-08:00","id":832114,"title":"","content":"Is Compromise still happening? Because that could radically change the answers to this question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T15:25:03-08:00","id":832119,"title":"","content":"Well, you could argue that &quot;Going Loud&quot; would enable demons to recharge. But that raises the new problem: managing your fellow demons. It almost becomes like Vampire in that the fear of drawing attention from Hunters, other splats, and militant Exiles still faithful to the GM becomes paramount.<br /> <br /> Edit: but yeah, Compromise still occurs. Just no angels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":974,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","user":"MrParaduo","date":". 02-17-2016, 06:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T15:37:29-08:00","id":832127,"title":"","content":"Full crossover? Because without the G-M's angelic legions, or other roughly equally powered splats, Demons have a huge power boost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T15:44:45-08:00","id":832134,"title":"","content":"Not necessarily. Demons fighting against demons, their progeny, and endowed hunters. But yeah, probably a cross-over setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T15:49:39-08:00","id":832139,"title":"","content":"Yeah, those *can* pose a threat, but a decent demon seriously out guns them when they don't have to worry about Compromise.<br /> <br /> Of course, no Angels means no new Demons...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T16:27:45-08:00","id":832163,"title":"","content":"Without the G-M Offspring and Fractals wouldn't get their interlocks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T16:50:19-08:00","id":832184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/832092-if-demons-won-the-war?p=832163#post832163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without the G-M Offspring and Fractals wouldn't get their interlocks.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. True.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T17:13:04-08:00","id":832198,"title":"","content":"All of the above.<br /> <br /> <b>Short Term Analysis:</b> The Tempters will throw a party... a really, really big party. They're probably the best off of the four agendas, they're now free to enjoy the world however they want.<br /> <br /> The Saboteurs will show up, and as the party goes on, they'll realize that the defining aspect of there existence is... gone. Cue existential crisis.<br /> <br /> The Inquisitors will go deep shadow, hiding from even their own Rings and Agencies. They will assume (and most certainly be correct) that the G-m's disappearance is either a) a ruse, or b) a sign of something very, very bad to come. After all, the G-M does protect humanity from extinction, and that's not a responsibility that the Unchained (or anyone else) are prepared to take up. Also, as the Paranoids are the ones most likely to be able to create their own infrastructure, they'll be in high demand. What they can do is a pale imitation of the G-m's own capabilities, but Aether is Aether. In any case, their priority becomes finding out what happened to the G-M... and what will happen to earth with it gone? Will one the Idigem, which the Unchained believe to be embryonic forms of the G-M, grow to full maturity? Is there some other entity that G-m was holding at bay? Was the G-m called home (maybe it really was an AI on a crashed alien space ship)? Which brings us to...<br /> <br /> The Integrators will also be trying to find out what happened to the G-M, but for different reasons. If the G-M is in distress, or is disabled, this is a golden opportunity for a group of integrators to prove themselves worthy to their former master. For all they know, this could be the G-M ordained meaning of their descent: to provide aid in its most dire need, an idea that will certainly appeal to to Integrators. For those so inclined, this is also the time to get access to the G-m diagnostic/repair/ reset functions to kill three birds with one stone: get the G-M back, make sure it's sane in the process, and get in it's good graces.<br /> <br /> <b>Long Term Analysis:</b> without the threat of the G-M's hunters, demons will become less cautious about their actions, the most experienced and disciplined will stick to the shadows, but for many more, the temptation to live a normal life, to finally be honest with spouses, family and friends with will grow with every day that there is no response from the G-M. This new found freedom will cause he Unchained will start interacting with other splats more as they expand into new territory, much like a species of animal that has just seen its primary predator go extinct.<br /> <br /> Other supernatural splats will start to have trouble maintaining their own secrecy, as in the GMC- continuity, the G-M's concealment Infrastructure plays a large part in keeping the Masquerade running. The supernatural eventually goes public.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","user":"Agentwestmer","date":". 02-17-2016, 09:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T18:11:41-08:00","id":832219,"title":"","content":"I could see that turning into the End of Days.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T20:38:38-08:00","id":832299,"title":"","content":"I can imagine the Saboteurs, after deciding on backup plans for the possible return of the G-M, will change their focus into protecting themselves and each from the other splats. Their list of preferred tactics wouldn't suffer a drastic overhaul, but they would need more info on these new threats that take the place of the G-M as obstacles to their Hells.<br /> <br /> Rings of Saboteurs and Inquisitors would increase significantly in number, as each Agenda turns to the other for intelligence gathering and manpower. Without the G-M's Concealment Infrastructure, a new Agenda might emerge with the goal of upholding an unstable Masquerade and using diplomacy with the other monsters.<br /> <br /> Since no more Angels are being constructed, that means the population of Demons will only decrease. Demons would invest more resources into missions for causing Exiles to Fall and join them. The truly desperate would initiate secret research on how to build more Demons using the powers and parts of other monsters. Even so, every attempt to bring an ally into the world would be a very calculated risk, as Demons would still be paranoid about betrayal.<br /> <br /> The <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/624337-analyst-issues-incarnations-infrastructure-types-and-agendas-new-style-soon/page2\"><b>Inventors</b></a> would have a spike in requests for membership, as they were the ones with the biggest hoards and understanding of Infrastructure. They may look to the many types of ephemeral beings in order to synthesize Angelic Essence and thus Aether. Research on the Divine Fire and its Qashmallim would become one of their priorities, due to similarities between the latter and G-M Angels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T23:33:30-08:00","id":832354,"title":"","content":"Dark Eras (After the Fall) deals with a more localised, less extreme version of this. Hopefully it'll be released soon.<br /> <br /> I agree with the sudden spike in inter-demon conflict as resources become scarse and they attempt to build incompatible Hells. Integrators and Saboteurs are going to suffer existential crises. And, as some people have mentioned, some of many plates the God-Machine keeps spinning are going to be dropped and smashed. For example, without regular suicide-sacrifices, you can expect a lot of earthquakes and volcanic activity around Mt Fuji. Demons are the best equipped to step up to the role and take on the burden of maintaining such vital Infrastructure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T23:51:30-08:00","id":832362,"title":"","content":"Metal Gear Solid 4: The Guns of the God Machine <br /> <br /> More seriously though... It could be an amazing setting in its own right. <br /> <br /> I would run the major agendas and agencies exploring the &quot;Corpse&quot; of God, its infrastructure and hidden realms. After much much chaos, these Agencies would need to form some sort of political order that could maintain whatever functions of the God Machine would be necessary or desirable. Every Angel would become an Exile, and would basically need to be recruited by Demons to do things. The source of conflict here is getting Qashmallim, spirits, ghosts, old exiles, and the newer kinds of exiles to behave properly. If the Pentacle or Seers support this celestial government, at this point Demon's are running a Celestial Bureaucracy, and we have Exalted in the Chronicles of Darkness. <br /> <br /> Things Demons do in this setting, and could each be an Agenda which spawns from one of the original four, or any of these tasks may be based on incarnations as well:<br /> <br /> Maintaining reality<br /> Figuring out if the God Machine existed in outer space or had interacted with extraterrestrials of any kind. <br /> Keeping out things from the lower depths and abyss<br /> maintaining the secrecy of the supernatural from humans<br /> monitoring the ephemeral and invisible realms<br /> Politics involving Mages<br /> Manipulating hunters<br /> Maintaining Demonic bloodlines. <br /> Hunting &quot;Radicals&quot;/&quot;Reactionaries&quot; who disagree with the new system. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8619-aforgeforthoughts","name":"AForgeForThoughts","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T18:31:30-08:00","id":832918,"title":"","content":"I always imagine that if the Demons &quot;won&quot; then the Integrators would be the most interesting hook - like, I imagine they'd start work on building a new God Machine so they could go home, or reviving it, or reconciling time splinters where it still exists with the 'main' timeline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T19:13:01-08:00","id":832947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/832092-if-demons-won-the-war?p=832918#post832918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always imagine that if the Demons &quot;won&quot; then the Integrators would be the most interesting hook - like, I imagine they'd start work on building a new God Machine so they could go home, or reviving it, or reconciling time splinters where it still exists with the 'main' timeline.</div> </div> </div> </div>My personal preference in that scenario is a messianic figure, a Demon who claims to be the Fallen God-Machine Itself, who starts rallying loyal Integrators to its banner so that they can return to Heaven.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T19:35:21-08:00","id":832957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/832092-if-demons-won-the-war?p=832947#post832947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My personal preference in that scenario is a messianic figure, a Demon who claims to be the Fallen God-Machine Itself, who starts rallying loyal Integrators to its banner so that they can return to Heaven.</div> </div> </div> </div> Plot twist; they're actually an old, insane Saboteur who adopted this persona in the mad hope it would give their fellow Soldiers a new purpose. <br /> <br /> Probably a stupid idea, but one I find interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T21:33:46-08:00","id":833013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/832092-if-demons-won-the-war?p=832110#post832110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't it become one hell of a struggle for dwindling resources, as all the Infrastructure slowly crumbles without repair? Aether is practically the lifeblood of the Unchained, and unless someone finds a way to build new Infrastructure without the Machine it'll quickly run out.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a process that lets demons gather aether from the sun. They could build an entire economy around spreading that aether.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T21:47:36-08:00","id":833020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/832092-if-demons-won-the-war?p=832957#post832957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Plot twist; they're actually an old, insane Saboteur who adopted this persona in the mad hope it would give their fellow Soldiers a new purpose.<br /> <br /> Probably a stupid idea, but one I find interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not as bad as you think. Reintegrating soldiers (small 's') into society has always been a challenge. For the most part, it happens, especially if the soldier in question has a solid support network (something like 97% of Vietnam veterans were able to reintegrate successfully, for this reason).<br /> <br /> Saboteurs are the <i>least</i> likely of any agenda to have a family or other support network, do to a combination of Burning Covers as the G-M catches up with them, and Going Loud to fight back (though exceptions exist, as they always do). That, and they've been fighting a war that few can truly understand, sometimes for centuries. Now, they've lost the very lynchpin of their existence, and in a way that denies true closure: The G-M hasn't been slain, it just <i>left</i>, as if all those centuries of effort, sacrifice, Burnt families and dead friends was for nothing.<br /> <br /> I can completely imagine some Saboteurs making very questionable and self-destructive decisions, just to maintain some sort of relevance in their lives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T21:48:11-08:00","id":833021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\